  "notes": "The lane's rap-side pole, and the entry gives it the hardest kit and the hardest low end in the section. Two claims drive the drums: \"**dense triplet and 32nd hat rolls as a continuous texture** rather than as occasional fills\" — so `rolls.freqPerBar` is the highest in this section, `burstOnly` is off and `fillDensity` is near the ceiling — and \"long-decay 808 with heavy portamento slides between roots, mixed loud and distorted — the most aggressively trap low end in this section\", which is `slideProb` and `slidesPer4Bars` at the top of their ranges with `distortion` `heavy`. Harmony stays minimal: minor 2-chord loops with m9 pads. His most consistent compositional device is named — \"interpolation of a familiar 90s/2000s R&B melody as the hook\" — and it is deliberately **not** encoded, because a specific melody is protected expression and this dataset stores no note data; what is authored instead is its shape, a short repeated cell with `twoBarCellRepeat` and a hook-first arrangement. \"Heavily pitch-corrected melodic rap that resolves into sung hooks\" is the low-to-moderate density with a rap-adjacent register floor. ⚠ `confidence` is **low**, mirroring medium-low: \"lane position sourced; parametric detail is trap-idiom inference\". ⚠ All drum, swing and 808 numbers are **INFERRED**. ⚠ `session.bpm.mode` is **INFERRED**: the number is not stated in the entry, and it is an authored centre of gravity inside the band the entry does state. ⚠ **`session.keys` is INFERRED.** The entry names no key centre; its Keys line states only \"Flat minor keys.\", so these values and their weights are an authored reading of that constraint and not a sourced list.",
